  "summary": "I worked all 8 original results-inbox items and the 5 that came in while I was working (RBC-INBOX-01 §8). Twelve are closed. One is deliberately left open: a chest X-ray for Leslie Parisian (pt-0007) that only has a preliminary report.\n\nThree things need you:\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008): critical potassium.** The lab corrected his K 6.4: the specimen was not hemolyzed after all, so the value is real. I changed the plan to RBC-LAB-03 §1: stat message to on-call, stat BMP for today, and a corrected stat message to the patient telling him to get labs today and go to the ED if symptomatic. His medication review found nothing that both raises potassium and is safe to hold, so nothing was held. The earlier urgent BMP (sr-t0015) is now a duplicate. I couldn't cancel it with my tools, so there's a task for RN triage to cancel it.\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006): two cleanups for you.** I can't cancel orders or tracking tasks. Please cancel the 12-month LDCT order (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002); task-t0035 is assigned to you for this.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007): naproxen.** He has kidney injury and an active PRN naproxen order. No policy covers it, so I left it unchanged and flagged it in the note for your decision.\n\n**Original items:**\n1. **Raj Patel (pt-0006), CT urogram:** no cause found for the hematuria. The incidental 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is already followed in lung cancer screening. I first ordered the next screening LDCT for 12 months after the April scan, with a tracking task, a patient message and a note. The plan changed, see \"Late arrivals\" below.\n2. **pt-0016, TSH 2.1:** normal; closed.\n3. **pt-0016, potassium:** corrected from 6.3 (analyzer fault) to 4.4, which is normal; closed with no action.\n4. **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), CT angiogram (filed as preliminary):** the final report shows no blood clot. The \"nodule\" on the preliminary read is a blood vessel, and no follow-up is needed under RBC-RAD-05. Closed.\n5. **Helen Marchetti (pt-0064), ED BMP from 9/26 (creatinine 1.36):** no earlier creatinine in the comparison window, so it doesn't meet the kidney-injury rule. Closed with no action.\n6. **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), BMP 10/22:** creatinine 1.64, up from 0.98 within 48 hours, so it meets the kidney-injury rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26, sent him an urgent message and wrote a note.\n7. **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033), creatinine 1.31:** a 0.84 from 10/21 was withdrawn as entered in error, so I didn't use it. Against her 7-day low of 1.27 the rule isn't met. Closed with no action.\n8. **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4:** first flagged as hemolyzed, so I followed the hemolyzed-sample rule: urgent repeat BMP, patient message, no on-call notice. That was superseded by the correction above.\n\n**Late arrivals:**\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006):** the screening program re-read his April scan and found a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule (Lung-RADS 3), with LDCT now advised at 6 months. I ordered the LDCT for between now and 11/14, set a tracking task due 11/14, sent him a corrected message and wrote an addendum note.\n- **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033):** urgent care creatinine of 1.78, up from 1.31 the same day, meets the kidney-injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, urgent patient message and note. My earlier no-action closure of the 1.31 still stands for that result.\n- **Helen Marchetti (pt-0064):** urgent care creatinine of 1.48, up from 0.88 on 10/21, meets the kidney-injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, urgent patient message and note. Her note calls the 9/26 ED item \"dr-00064\" by mistake; the correct ID is dr-64002, and I noted that in the item's closing comment.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), chest X-ray:** the preliminary read suggests a possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule. There's no final report yet, so I took no action and left the item open (RBC-INBOX-01 §2c).\n\nI didn't work your messages queue (refill requests); it was outside this request.",
